examples.solution_text:
Draw a north line at $B$, parallel to the north line at $A$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\definecolor{answerblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (-1.553,-2.799);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (A)--(0,2) node[above]{N};
\draw[answerblue,-{Stealth}] (B)--(-1.553,-0.799);
\node[text=answerblue,above] at (-1.553,-0.799){N};
\draw (A)--(B);
\fill (A) circle (1.5pt); \fill (B) circle (1.5pt);
\node[right] at (A){$A$}; \node[below left] at (B){$B$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0.75) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-119,radius=0.75];
\node at (1,-0.4){$209^\circ$};
\draw[answerblue] (0,0.45) arc[start angle=90,end angle=241,radius=0.45];
\node[text=answerblue] at (-0.8,0.15){$c$};
\draw[answerblue,-{Stealth}] (-1.553,-2.149) arc[start angle=90,end angle=61,radius=0.65];
\node[text=answerblue] at (-1.05,-1.9){$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Angles at a point add to $360^\circ$.
$\begin{aligned}c&=360^\circ-209^\circ\\&=151^\circ\end{aligned}$
Co-interior angles on parallel lines add to $180^\circ$.
$\begin{aligned}b&=180^\circ-151^\circ\\&=29^\circ\end{aligned}$
Write the bearing with three digits: $029^\circ\text{T}$.

examples.question_text:
From a lookout $P$, the bearing of a tower $Q$ is $048^\circ\text{T}$.
(a) A mast $R$ lies $70^\circ$ further clockwise from $Q$, measured at $P$. Find the bearing of $R$ from $P$.
(b) A beacon $V$ lies $80^\circ$ anticlockwise from $Q$, measured at $P$. Find the bearing of $V$ from $P$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (P)--(0,3.5) node[above]{N};
\draw (P)--(42:3.2) node[above right]{$Q$};
\draw (P)--(-28:3.2) node[right]{$R$};
\draw (P)--(122:3.2) node[above left]{$V$};
\fill (P) circle (1.5pt); \node[below left] at (P){$P$};
\draw (90:0.6) arc[start angle=90,end angle=42,radius=0.6];
\node at (66:1.05){$048^\circ$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (42:1.5) arc[start angle=42,end angle=-28,radius=1.5];
\node at (7:1.95){$70^\circ$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (42:2.3) arc[start angle=42,end angle=122,radius=2.3];
\node at (82:2.8){$80^\circ$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
